<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obersalzberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Obersalzberg is a mountainside above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berchtesgaden">Berchtesgaden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavarian-alps">Bavarian Alps</a>. From the 1920s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> stayed there, and after 1933 the area was turned into a fenced compound with his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berghof">Berghof</a>, houses for Nazi leaders, barracks and the Kehlsteinhaus on the summit above. Most of the buildings were bombed in 1945 and later cleared, and a documentation centre on the Nazi period opened there in 1999.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obersalzberg.jpg" alt="Obersalzberg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tobi85 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_Kehlsteinstra%C3%9Fe1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
